---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, SITE_URL, addressLines } from '../data/site';

/**
 * Content follows the supplied terms-and-conditions document.
 *
 * Two placeholders in the source were resolved and one was deliberately not:
 *  - "[Insert Website URL]" → SITE_URL.
 *  - "[Insert Jurisdiction/State/Country]" → Chandigarh, India, inferred from
 *    the registered business address.
 *  - The late-payment clause read "a late fee of ___ per month" with the figure
 *    missing. A percentage is NOT invented here; the clause defers to the
 *    service agreement instead. See docs/brand-and-content-analysis.md §12.
 */
const host = SITE_URL.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');
---

<Legal
  title="Terms & conditions"
  metaTitle={`Terms & conditions — ${site.name}`}
  description={`The terms governing use of the ${site.name} website and our digital marketing services.`}
  lead={`By using this website or engaging our services, you agree to the terms below. Please read them carefully.`}
  updated="12 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    Welcome to {site.legalName}. By accessing our website at
    <a href={SITE_URL}>{host}</a> or engaging our digital marketing services, you agree
    to comply with and be bound by the following terms and conditions.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Introduction and acceptance of terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms and conditions govern your use of the {site.legalName} website and all
    digital marketing services provided by {site.legalName} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;,
    &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;). By accessing our platform or entering into a
    service agreement with us, you accept these terms in full. If you disagree with any
    part of these terms, you must not use our website or services.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Digital marketing services</h2>
  <h3>Scope of work</h3>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} provides digital marketing services including, but not limited to,
    search engine optimisation (SEO), pay-per-click (PPC) advertising, social media
    management, content creation, email marketing and web design. The specific scope,
    deliverables and timelines will be outlined in a separate statement of work (SOW) or
    service agreement.
  </p>
  <h3>Results and performance</h3>
  <p>
    While we employ industry best practices to achieve optimal results, digital marketing
    outcomes depend heavily on third-party platforms (such as Google, Meta and LinkedIn)
    and on market dynamics. {site.legalName} therefore does not guarantee specific search
    engine rankings, lead volumes or revenue increases.
  </p>
  <h3>Third-party platforms</h3>
  <p>
    Our strategies may involve managing accounts on third-party platforms. Clients are
    subject to the terms of service of those respective platforms.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Intellectual property rights</h2>
  <h3>Our content</h3>
  <p>
    All content on the {site.legalName} website — including text, graphics, logos, icons,
    images, audio clips and software — is the property of {site.legalName} and protected
    by international copyright and intellectual property laws.
  </p>
  <h3>Client materials</h3>
  <p>
    You retain ownership of all intellectual property rights in the logos, brand assets
    and content you provide to us for use in marketing campaigns. You grant
    {' '}{site.legalName} a non-exclusive, worldwide licence to use, reproduce and display
    these materials solely for the purpose of executing the agreed services.
  </p>
  <h3>Deliverables</h3>
  <p>
    Upon full payment of all applicable fees, ownership of final customised deliverables
    — such as ad creatives, custom graphics and written copy — transfers to the client,
    excluding proprietary agency frameworks, tools or software.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Payment terms</h2>
  <h3>Invoicing</h3>
  <p>
    Fees for ongoing services are billed in advance on a monthly or milestone basis, as
    specified in your service agreement. Project-based work typically requires an upfront
    deposit before work commences.
  </p>
  <h3>Late payments</h3>
  <p>
    Invoices unpaid past the due date may incur a late fee at the rate set out in your
    service agreement, or the maximum allowed by law, whichever is lower.
    {' '}{site.legalName} reserves the right to suspend services until overdue accounts are
    settled in full.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, {site.legalName} shall not be
    liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages,
    including loss of profits, data, use or goodwill, or other intangible losses,
    resulting from your use of our website or services, or from any unauthorised access
    to or alteration of your transmissions or data.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of
    Chandigarh, India, without regard to its conflict of law provisions. Any legal action
    or proceeding arising under these terms shall be brought exclusively in the courts
    located within that jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Contact</h2>
  <p>For any questions or requests regarding these terms, please contact us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
    <li>Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phoneIntl}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a></li>
  </ul>
  <address>
    {addressLines.map((line) => <span>{line}</span>)}
  </address>
</Legal>
